<BaseLayout
  title="About The P List — Why We Celebrate Australia's Weirdest Homes"
  description="The P List exists for one reason: the houses with the most personality almost never get the photos they deserve. Here's why we find them, film them, and write them up."
  path="/about"
>
  <div class="wrap about-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>About the list</span>
    <h1 data-reveal style="margin-top:14px;transition-delay:60ms">We champion the houses<br />everyone else scrolls past.</h1>
    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:120ms">The P List exists for one reason: the houses with the most personality almost never get the photos they deserve. The avocado bathrooms. The pebblecrete. The carpet that's seen things. We find them, film them, and give them the affectionate write-up they've earned.</p>
    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:170ms"><strong>Properties that didn't make the A-list. But should have.</strong> That's the whole pitch.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:220ms">Let's be clear about what we're not, because people keep assuming. We are not real estate agents. We are not a real estate company. Nobody here holds a licence, wants a licence, or gets a commission if your dream pebblecrete bungalow sells. We don't list, we don't sell, we don't represent vendors, and we definitely don't do open homes in a blazer. We just find these places, fall in love with them, and tell you why.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:250ms">What we <em>are</em> is a small, deeply biased appreciation society for houses that have character &mdash; the good kind and the "what were they thinking" kind, which are frequently the same house. We're talking weird floorplans, wonderful original features, genuinely historic homes, and anything that has somehow escaped the great beige flattening of modern renovation. If a house has been "greiged" within an inch of its life &mdash; every wall, every surface, every skerrick of personality sanded down to the same shade of real-estate-photo grey &mdash; it will not be on this list. We are aggressively, proudly anti-boring.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:270ms">Yes, the tone is sarcastic. We're not going to apologise for that. But underneath the jokes is a real fondness for these places &mdash; the shag pile, the mirrored feature walls, the internal water features nobody asked for. Someone loved this house enough to make these choices on purpose, and that deserves more than a bland listing description and fifteen identical staged photos. It deserves a write-up with some personality of its own.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:300ms">It started on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/christoradio" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:underline;">Instagram</a>, and it's still happening there every day &mdash; this is where those finds get room to breathe. The full video instead of fifteen seconds. Every photo instead of one. The story that never fit in a caption. Follow along over there for the daily finds; come here when you want to go deeper on one.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:330ms">Every house we feature gets a video, a write-up, a property file &mdash; and a link straight back to its real listing (handled by real, actual agents, doing their actual jobs). We're not here to replace them; we're here to send them the attention their listing's beige stock photos were never going to get on their own.</p>

    <p data-reveal style="transition-delay:360ms">A quick disclosure, because you deserve one: every video on this site is filmed, voiced and edited by an actual human (me, Christo). The write-ups are a different story &mdash; I set the framework, the voice and the tone, and AI does the actual writing, pulling it all together into the finished piece. I have a full-time job and a family, and there simply aren't enough hours to hand-write this much copy without one of those things suffering badly. Every blurb is reviewed by me and signed off by me before it goes anywhere near the site. If something's wrong or off-brand, that's on me, not the robot.</p>

    <a href="/" class="btn btn-solid" data-reveal style="transition-delay:390ms">Back to the list</a>
  </div>
  <NewsletterBand />
</BaseLayout>
